# ── Rust / Soroban ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Soroban writes a ledger snapshot per test run as a debugging aid. Their
# contents depend on which build profile produced the WASM, so committing them
# means a diff on every CI run that says nothing about the code.
test_snapshots/

# ── Node / Next.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
coverage/

# ── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env*.local
!.env.example

# ── Stellar CLI state — CONTAINS SECRET KEYS ─────────────────────────────────
# The scripts set XDG_CONFIG_HOME to ./.config, so the CLI keeps identities in
# this project rather than your home directory. That means the admin's 24-word
# seed phrase is a file inside this repo:
#
#     .config/stellar/identity/pact-deployer.toml
#
# Never remove these rules. Anyone who obtains that file controls the admin —
# they can pause the registry, rotate the admin away from you, and settle every
# dispute in every escrow you ever deployed.
.config/
.stellar/
.soroban/
# Belt and braces: no identity file escapes, wherever it ends up.
**/identity/*.toml

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# ── Vercel ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel
